    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 6th with an aggressive offensive setup, headlined by **Yordan Alvarez**, who anchors the roster with an elite 87.42 efficiency score. His matchup against Morris (20.25 xERA) provides the highest ceiling on the slate, capitalizing on a massive SP vulnerability. We are also leaning heavily into speed and leadoff production today; **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (76.77) and **Christian Yelich** (74.32) are prioritized due to their prime lineup positioning and favorable platoon matchups against Roupp and Agnos, respectively. **Trea Turner** (70.35) remains a mandatory start, with his speed-to-base potential amplified by Eisert\u2019s slow delivery, a critical factor given our strategic emphasis on scarce stolen bases.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision was bypassing **Nelson Velazquez** (56.76) on the bench. Despite his elite 0.478 xwOBA, the optimizer favored **Chase Meidroth** (57.69) and **Junior Caminero** (57.61) due to slightly more stable situational factors and order placement. While **Nelson Velazquez** offers significant pop, the consistency of the active lineup's projected plate appearances against their respective right-handed opponents proved decisive. We are also closely monitoring the performance of **Dillon Dingler** (43.78); despite a base projection that sits near our floor, the wind-out conditions and his presence in the #3 spot provide enough leverage to keep him active over the bench-bound **Caleb Durbin** (53.33) and **Casey Schmitt** (49.94), who could not overcome the negative SP skill delta in their specific matchups.\n\nRisks today are largely concentrated in the volatility of the mid-tier starters. While we are starting **Luke Raley** (64.85) against Montero, we must acknowledge the inherent ceiling pressure of placing **Colt Keith** (55.09) in the #7 hole against Miller. We remain confident in the current configuration, but we will be keeping **Jacob Gonzalez** and **Casey Schmitt** on high alert should any late-inning lineup substitutions occur, particularly if weather delays or defensive replacements compromise the anticipated efficiency of our middle-of-the-pack starters.",
